    {
      "id": "postgresql-read-coverage",
      "service": "database/postgresql",
      "enabled": true,
      "heavy": false,
      "_note": "COVERAGE-ONLY read lifecycle for postgresql id-bound GETs. Soft-captures an existing cluster_id (from /v1/clusters) and dbaas_engine_version_id (from /v1/engine-versions), then a probe_reads step exercises EVERY postgresql catalog GET whose path params are satisfied (replicas via cluster_id, engine-version properties via dbaas_engine_version_id, requests via a literal placeholder request_id) so each id-bound GET is CALLED and RECORDED under its own catalog key (a 4xx counts as covered). 100% read-only: every step optional + grouped, broad expect_status. requests/{request_id} is KNOWN-HARD: request_id is returned only by async ops and is not listable, so a literal placeholder id is used purely so the endpoint is reached (4xx expected).",
      "steps": [
        {
          "name": "list-clusters",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/v1/clusters",
          "expect_status": [
            200,
            400,
            404
          ],
          "optional": true,
          "group": "read-cov",
          "capture_soft": {
            "cluster_id": "$.contents[0].id"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "list-engine-versions",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/v1/engine-versions",
          "expect_status": [
            200,
            400,
            404
          ],
          "optional": true,
          "group": "read-cov",
          "capture_soft": {
            "dbaas_engine_version_id": "$.contents[0].id"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "get-cluster-replicas",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/v1/clusters/{cluster_id}/replicas",
          "expect_status": [
            200,
            400,
            404
          ],
          "optional": true,
          "group": "read-cov"
        },
        {
          "name": "get-engine-version-properties",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/v1/engine-versions/{dbaas_engine_version_id}/properties",
          "expect_status": [
            200,
            400,
            404
          ],
          "optional": true,
          "group": "read-cov"
        },
        {
          "name": "probe-reads",
          "probe_reads": {
            "cluster_id": "{cluster_id}",
            "dbaas_engine_version_id": "{dbaas_engine_version_id}",
            "request_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "postgresql-cluster-version-upgrade",
      "service": "database/postgresql",
      "enabled": true,
      "heavy": true,
      "_note": "HEAVY 2026-07-16 (svccov-pg session, owner-approved SCP_RUN_HEAVY): dedicated 1-cluster campaign for postgresql's residual gap keys that the main database-postgresql-cluster + postgresql-cluster-subops-a/b lifecycles (run earlier today, run 20260716-181204-4912, 37/49 keys 2xx) never reach: postgresqlpatchminorversion, postgresqlshowinstance, postgresqlmanualbackup, postgresqlremovebackuphistories (PF recheck), postgresqlunsetbackup (PF recheck), postgresqlregisterlogexportconfig/setlogexportconfig/unregisterlogexportconfig/exportlog (PF recheck chain). postgresql has NO major-version-upgrade endpoint (confirmed absent from the catalog, unlike mysql/mariadb) so this lifecycle only does the minor-patch axis. STRATEGY: live GET /v1/engine-versions 2026-07-16 shows TWO minors under the newest major (COMMUNITY 17: 17.7 newest, 17.6 next) -- this CONTRADICTS the a690 2026-07-16 note in knowledge/validated-facts.md claiming 'no second minor exists' (that finding was stale/mistaken, or based on always resending the cluster's OWN current version rather than checking the full engine-versions list). Create the cluster on the OLDER minor (COMMUNITY 17.6, via where_prefix major_version='COMMUNITY 17' nth=1) so postgresqlpatchminorversion has a genuinely NEWER same-major target (COMMUNITY 17.7, nth=0) to patch to -- avoids the known 'Unpatchable version' 400 that resending the current version produces. postgresqlshowinstance needs instance_name (a NAME not an id) captured from $.instance_groups[0].instances[0].name on the cluster detail. postgresqlmanualbackup takes no request body (path cluster_id only, per data/api_docs.json). postgresqlremovebackuphistories body is {backup_history_number: [string]} (confirmed correct key, NOT a typo -- data/api_docs.json backuphistorynumberrequest) populated with a REAL id captured from list-backup-histories after manual-backup; the mysql sibling proved this STILL 401s Dbaas.Unauthorized.AuthNFailed even with the correct key + a real id (run svccov-mysql today) -- same backup-family query-string HMAC signing PF as postgresqlunsetbackup (known_issues.json), so both are 1-shot PF rechecks here, not chased further. register-log-export-config is a confirmed-PF 500 ContactAdminForAssistance across ALL 5 DB engines including postgresql (knowledge/validated-facts.md 'DB register-log-export-config 500 = 백엔드 PF 확정', our input already eliminated as cause) -- set/export/unregister-log-export-config are structurally unreachable-2xx downstream of it (export additionally 400s Dbaas.InvalidLogType on an unregistered log_type even with a literal enum value, confirmed on the mysql sibling), so this lifecycle 1-shot rechecks the whole chain then treats it as blocked, not a body bug. C-group (postgresqlcreaterestore, postgresqlcreateotherregionreplica, postgresqlswitchovercluster) deliberately EXCLUDED: each needs its own extra billable cluster, a completed backup, or an ha_enabled=true cluster -- left as a follow-up lever, not attempted here to stay in the session's single-cluster/time budget. Own dedicated VPC/subnet (10.143.0.0/20) so this lifecycle never contends with the main database-postgresql-cluster (10.133), heavy-shared-dbaas/subops-a/b (10.134), mysql-cluster-version-upgrade (10.142), or mariadb-cluster-version-upgrade (10.144).",
      "steps": [
        {
          "name": "create-vpc",
          "service": "vpc",
          "method": "POST",
          "path": "/v1/vpcs",
          "json": {
            "name": "regrvpc{unique}",
            "description": "API regression PG version-upgrade",
            "cidr": "10.143.0.0/20",
            "tags": []
          },
          "capture": {
            "vpc_id": "$.vpc.id"
          },
          "expect_status": [
            200,
            201,
            202
          ],
          "cleanup": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "path": "/v1/vpcs/{vpc_id}",
            "service": "vpc"
          },
          "adopt": "vpc"
        },
        {
          "name": "wait-vpc",
          "service": "vpc",
